Then plan phase N through rdm's planning lane, and implement it yourself against the approved plan:
1. Using the Skill tool, run `rdm:dispatch-phase` with arguments `@RDM_ROADMAP@ N --plan-only --project @RDM_PROJECT@`. It plans and plan-reviews the phase and implements nothing.
2. Read the approved plan: `rdm plan list --implements phase/@RDM_ROADMAP@/N --status approved --project @RDM_PROJECT@ --format json`, then `rdm plan show <its slug> --project @RDM_PROJECT@`.
3. Remove the planning worktree, which holds no commits, so that the next checkpoint plans against the current `main`: `rdm worktree remove @RDM_ROADMAP@ --delete-branch --project @RDM_PROJECT@`.
